<section class="www-section" id="first-form">
  <header class="www-section-head">
    <div>
      <p class="hara-v2-kicker">01 · First form</p>
      <h2>Read the source before a runtime attaches.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      A Hara form is useful as text and data before it is executable. The live surface adds a named browser session; it does not replace the source, expected value, or documentation path.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="www-three-part-argument" aria-label="First form reading order">
    <article><span>Definition</span><h3>Operation first</h3><p>Parentheses hold a computation, vectors hold ordered values, and maps name facts.</p></article>
    <article><span>Inspection</span><h3>Values stay close</h3><p>Evaluate a form, inspect the value, and change the program without translating it into another model.</p></article>
    <article><span>Runtime</span><h3>Execution is explicit</h3><p>The browser card names its kernel boundary and remains optional to the surrounding explanation.</p></article>
  </div>

  <div class="www-live-example">
    <header class="www-live-example__header">
      <div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Browser kernel</p><h3>Read, transform, and inspect a value</h3></div>
      <span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="success">Runnable</span>
    </header>
    <div class="www-live-example__contract">
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Web · interpreter core</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Session</dt><dd>Homepage scoped</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Network</dt><dd>None required</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <span>Source remains visible while the kernel loads.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="www-live-example__workspace">
      <div class="www-live-example__mount" data-live-learn>
        <div class="www-static-example" data-live-fallback>
          <div><span>read.hal</span><small>Static source</small></div>
          <pre><code>(+ 19 23)</code></pre>
          <p><span>Expected value</span><code>42</code></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <span>Four reading rules</span>
        <strong>Operation first.</strong>
        <p>Code remains ordinary structure that the runtime, tools, tests, and people can inspect without a second representation.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <footer class="www-live-example__footer">
      <span>Runtime assets load after the document.</span>
      <a href="/docs/learn-programming/">Learn to read Hara →</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</section>
